      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/metynnis_fasciatus_breeding_coloration_en/",
      "html": "<p>Metynnis fasciatus is a very rarely offered silver dollar which has a characteristic zebra pattern.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/metynnis_fasciatus_breeding_coloration_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males and females can be easily distinguished in all Metynnis by the shape of the anal fin, which is straight bordered in females and has a lappet-like extension in males.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/metynnis_fasciatus_breeding_coloration_en/",
      "html": "<p>The breeding coloration of the males was observed for the first time ever in one of the tanks. The males look fantastic with their pitch-black face mask.</p>"
    }
  ],
